@startuml
title playback-from-logs: Full Replay Flow\n(python -m app playback-from-logs --path ./results/batch_...)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5

participant "__main__" as CLI
participant "FileOps" as FO
participant "ReplayRunner" as RR
participant "MatplotlibAnimator" as Renderer

== Load ==

CLI -> FO: load_batch_replay(path)

FO -> FO: Read metadata.json
note right of FO
    metadata contains:
    - total episodes in batch
    - replay_freq used at save time
    - per-episode: index, policy_name,
      timesteps, sim_speed_multiplier
end note

FO -> FO: Read step_data.npz
note right of FO
    .npz contains frame arrays:
    episode_0_frames (n, H, W, 3)
    episode_5_frames (n, H, W, 3)
    episode_10_frames (n, H, W, 3)
    ...
end note

FO -> FO: Build BatchReplay\n(EpisodeReplay per saved episode)
FO --> CLI: BatchReplay

== Initialise Display ==

CLI -> Renderer: MatplotlibAnimator()
CLI -> RR: ReplayRunner(renderer)

== Replay ==

CLI -> RR: replay_batch(batch_replay)

loop for each EpisodeReplay in batch_replay.episodes

    RR -> RR: Log "Replaying episode {index}\n({timesteps} steps, {speed}× speed)"

    note over RR
        sim_speed_multiplier read from
        episode metadata — no CLI override
    end note

    RR -> RR: tick = MODEL_TICK / metadata.sim_speed_multiplier

    ref over RR, Renderer: See: sd_playback_episode.puml

    RR -> RR: Log "Episode {index} complete"
end

RR --> CLI: done
CLI -> Renderer: quit()

@enduml
